casecards=''.join('<article class="case" id="case-%s"><div class="case-heading"><span class="case-code">%s</span><h4>%s</h4></div><p>%s</p><div class="case-image"><img src="topologies/%s.svg" alt="%s topology diagram" loading="lazy"></div><a href="topologies/%s.svg">Open full-size diagram ↗</a></article>' % (x['id'],x['id'],html.escape(x['name']),html.escape(x['description']),x['id'],html.escape(x['id']),x['id']) for x in topology)
caseindex=''.join('<a href="#case-%s">%s</a>'%(x['id'],x['id']) for x in topology)
caseview='''<section class="article" id="test-paths"><div class="section-kicker">EXPERIMENT DESIGN / OCT 2026</div><h2>Test paths &amp; topologies</h2><p>These diagrams describe historical test layouts using anonymized node labels. The diagrams show logical topology, not proof of offload.</p><h3>How the matrix was designed</h3><div class="case-image overview"><img src="topologies/overview.svg" alt="Test design overview: topology families, mode choices, possible CPU, Linux, CPPE and NSS paths, and evidence checks"></div><p>The T and W matrices each covered 240 cases in the NSS 12.5 campaign. D0 was the two-WLAN control; D1–D4 were an NSS 12.5 extension, with 199/200 selected extension and control cases passing functionality and quality. An L2 bridge test is a separate control. The historical report also records failures and unqualified attempts; these are not Image 12 qualification results.</p><p>In hardware-requested mode, acceptance and ownership vary: for example, W1 mixed Wi-Fi flows showed NSS activity despite CPPE steering rejection. T1 demonstrated directional CPPE admission asymmetry. Do not infer one engine from a topology diagram or from the hardware-offload flag alone.</p><div class="case-index">'''+caseindex+'''</div><div class="cases">'''+casecards+'''</div></section>'''
lineage_json=json.dumps(registry['images']).replace('<','\u003c')
lineage='''<section class="article" id="lineage"><div class="section-kicker">BUILD HISTORY / EARLY GRAPH + LATER RECORDS</div><h2>Explore the image lineage</h2><p>Follow the colored commit lanes to see the upstream bases, NSS integration and native build variants. Select a commit for its source, patch families and outcome; use the filters to highlight matching images. The legend distinguishes recorded parent sources from integration relationships and same-source build variants. Source commits alone do not capture every overlay or local build delta.</p>'''+render((root/'recent-lineage.md').read_text())+'''<div class="lineage-filters"><label>Acceleration <select id="filter-accel"><option value="all">All modes</option><option value="native">Native / control</option><option value="nss">Wi-Fi NSS</option><option value="failed">NSS startup failed</option></select></label><label>OpenWrt base <select id="filter-base"><option value="all">All bases</option><option value="a516fe3151ab">a516fe3151ab · 6.18.55</option><option value="d13ba979b017">d13ba979b017 · 6.18.60</option><option value="39e77cc05db9">39e77cc05db9 · 6.18.60</option></select></label><label>Patch theme <select id="filter-theme"><option value="all">All themes</option><option value="nss">NSS integration</option><option value="edma">EDMA integration</option><option value="mtu">MTU</option><option value="lifetime">Lifetime / teardown</option><option value="modules">Network modules</option><option value="ramoops">Ramoops capture</option></select></label><button id="reset-filters" type="button">Reset</button></div><p id="lineage-count" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="lineage-graph"></div><script type="application/json" id="lineage-data">'''+lineage_json+'''</script></section>'''
timeline=''.join('<details><summary><span class="num">%02d</span><span><b>%s</b><small>%s · Linux %s</small></span></summary><p>%s</p><p class="meta">Source <code>%s</code> · %s</p></details>' % (x['image_number'],html.escape(x['title']),html.escape(x['built_date']),html.escape(x['linux_kernel']),html.escape(x.get('comments','')),html.escape(x.get('source_commit','')[:12]),html.escape(x.get('runtime_status',''))) for x in registry['images'])
diagrams=(root/'diagrams.html').read_text()
board='''<section class="article" id="board"><div class="section-kicker">HARDWARE / CONCEPTUAL</div><h2>Inside the router</h2><p>Bus-level architecture of the board: the integrated 5 GHz radio (phy0, ath11k_ahb) and the discrete PCIe 5 GHz radio (phy2, ath11k_pci) are separate subsystems, each with its own RF path. The integrated subsystem also supplies the 2.4 GHz radio (phy1). The inventory identifies the PCIe radio by its QCN9074 driver family; the <a href="https://openwrt.org/toh/hwdata/jdcloud/jdcloud_re-cs-02">OpenWrt hardware record</a> describes related radio part numbers. Confirm chip markings and board revision before treating these names as interchangeable.</p><div class="case-image overview"><img src="topologies/board.svg" alt="Conceptual router block diagram"></div><p>See the <a href="https://note88.cn/archives/29188">community AX6600 teardown photographs ↗</a> and the <a href="https://git.openwrt.org/project/firmware/qca-wireless/tree/">OpenWrt board-data repository ↗</a>. External photographs remain on their publisher’s site.</p><p>The <a href="https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/blob/main/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq6010-re-cs-02.dts">board device tree ↗</a> records the PCIe endpoint, Ethernet port/PHY mapping and PCS modes. The <a href="https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/blob/main/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq6010-re-cs.dtsi">shared board description ↗</a> records the 8-bit eMMC controller, USB and QCA8075 PHY package. These upstream links track main; lab radio names are recorded runtime identities. RF companion chip markings, antenna routing and PCIe negotiated rate are not established by the diagram.</p></section>'''
nav=''.join('<a href="#%s">%s</a>'%(i,html.escape(t)) for i,t,_ in articles)
capture_diagram='<div class="diagrams"><div><small>CRASH EVIDENCE / RETENTION PATH</small><div class="flow"><span>Kernel fault<br><b>or console output</b></span><i>→</i><span>Ramoops<br><b>reserved DDR</b></span><i>→ reset / boot →</i><span>Pstore<br><b>recovered records</b></span><i>→</i><span>Archive service<br><b>eMMC + hashes</b></span></div><p>Reserved RAM retention depends on reset behavior. External p43 netconsole provides independent evidence; neither path guarantees capture of every fault.</p></div></div>'
sections=''.join('<section class="article" id="%s">%s</section>'%(i,(body+capture_diagram if i=='08-crash-capture' else body)) for i,_,body in articles)
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Public summaries of JDCloud AX6600 OpenWrt development, architecture and results."><title>AX6600 Field Notes</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body><header><a class="brand" href="#top"><span>◈</span> AX6600 <em>FIELD NOTES</em></a><a class="header-link" href="#03-journey">Explore the research ↗</a></header><main id="top"><section class="latest-update" aria-labelledby="latest-mesh-title"><div class="eyebrow">LATEST RESULTS · 16 NOVEMBER 2026, 19:19 SINGAPORE</div><h2 id="latest-mesh-title">802.11s mesh: channel 100 selected</h2><p>Channel 100 HE80 is the user-selected persistent mesh default; reviewed documentation supports retaining HE80.</p><a class="button" href="#11-mesh-20261116">Read mesh results and follow-up →</a></section><div class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">OPENWRT / IPQ601x / RE-CS-02</div><h1>From stock firmware<br>to <i>open ground.</i></h1><p>An evidence-led guide to the hardware, acceleration paths and experiments behind a mainstream OpenWrt build for the JDCloud AX6600.</p><div class="hero-links"><a class="button" href="#01-foundation">Start with the device →</a><a href="#timeline">View image timeline ↓</a></div></div><div class="board" aria-hidden="true"><div class="board-grid"><span>IPQ<br><b>601x</b></span><span>CPPE<br><b>FLOW</b></span><span>QCN<br><b>9074</b></span><span>eMMC<br><b>BOOT</b></span></div><div class="board-label">BOARD / SOFTWARE / EVIDENCE</div></div></div><div class="status"><div><small>DEVICE</small><strong>JDCloud RE-CS-02</strong></div><div><small>LATEST IMAGE RECORD</small><strong>#17 / #23 installed</strong></div><div><small>ACCELERATION</small><strong>Wi-Fi NSS + CPPE</strong></div><div><small>RECORD THROUGH</small><strong>16 Nov 2026</strong></div></div><div class="layout"><aside><div class="aside-label">THE KNOWLEDGE BASE</div>'''+nav+'''<a href="#board">Router components</a><a href="#lab-topology">Lab network</a><a href="#test-paths">Test paths &amp; topologies</a><a href="#issues">Issues &amp; fixes</a><a href="#cppe-lifecycle">CPPE flow lifecycle</a><a href="#lineage">Image lineage explorer</a><a href="#timeline">Image timeline</a><p>Claims are scoped to the recorded image and experiment. Only summaries, conclusions and aggregate results are published here.</p></aside><div class="content"><div class="intro"><span>FIELD GUIDE / EVIDENCE THROUGH 16 NOV</span><p>Start with the board. Follow the packet. Trace the decisions.</p></div>'''+diagrams+board+sections+lab+caseview+issues+cppe+lineage+'''<section class="article" id="timeline"><h2>Image timeline</h2><p>The registry records distinct FIT variants. Open an entry for its role and qualification. A source commit alone may not include local build deltas.</p>'''+timeline+'''</section></div></div></main><footer><span>◈ &nbsp; AX6600 FIELD NOTES</span><span>Evidence over assumptions. · Public field notes</span></footer><script>document.querySelectorAll('aside a').forEach(a=>a.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.querySelectorAll('aside a').forEach(x=>x.classList.remove('active'));a.classList.add('active')}));</script><script src="lineage.js"></script><script src="cppe.js"></script></body></html>'''
